(4986018, 723471, 97166, '<td valign="top">Jasper ran from the lighthouse bay, as fast as his feet would take him. His heart felt ready to burst, but he knew he had to make the radio before they struck. His feet barely touched the stairs as he descended.  Half way down he heard it. The first of the sounds, sounds he knew were not so distant explosions. "NO!" he cried as he somehow found the strength to go faster. Somehow found the dexterity to leap more stairs at a time without slipping and breaking his neck, ensuring that it would all end without anyone else the wiser.<br/> <br/>Jasper leapt the final stair, and burst through the door into the communications room, but it was too late.  They were there before him. Those repulsive beings. They who came in the stars.  Jasper screamed as he lunged for the radio, trying in spite of the odds to send one final warning, his hand stretched out in definance.<br/> <br/>Somewhere, inland, in a lonely room under eighty feet of earth, the screams were heard.</td>', 'Jasper ran from the lighthouse bay, as fast as his feet would take him. His heart felt ready to burst, but he knew he had to make the radio before they struck. His feet barely touched the stairs as he descended.  Half way down he heard it. The first of the sounds, sounds he knew were not so distant explosions. "NO!" he cried as he somehow found the strength to go faster. Somehow found the dexterity to leap more stairs at a time without slipping and breaking his neck, ensuring that it would all end without anyone else the wiser. Jasper leapt the final stair, and burst through the door into the communications room, but it was too late.  They were there before him. Those repulsive beings. They who came in the stars.  Jasper screamed as he lunged for the radio, trying in spite of the odds to send one final warning, his hand stretched out in definance. Somewhere, inland, in a lonely room under eighty feet of earth, the screams were heard.', '2008-10-01 23:31:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(4986021, 725055, 97166, '<td valign="top">Gus pouted.  It''s not like he could do much more, his eyes forever set in such an expression.  When Gus was promised reincarnation, his wildest dreams weren''t enough to prepare him for this.  In his former life, his lips had never been touched by a woman, and he had been promised that his new life would be different.  Now, they were touched all too often, but this wasn''t what he had had in mind. This gross distortion of his being, doomed to life as a steering wheel and a set of dash instruments, and he can''t even say what they do to his...<br/> <br/>Gus pouted.  It was not as if he could do much else.</td>', 'Gus pouted.  It''s not like he could do much more, his eyes forever set in such an expression.  When Gus was promised reincarnation, his wildest dreams weren''t enough to prepare him for this.  In his former life, his lips had never been touched by a woman, and he had been promised that his new life would be different.  Now, they were touched all too often, but this wasn''t what he had had in mind. This gross distortion of his being, doomed to life as a steering wheel and a set of dash instruments, and he can''t even say what they do to his... Gus pouted.  It was not as if he could do much else.', '2008-10-01 23:35:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(4986025, 724403, 97166, '<td valign="top">In all their years, the trees had never seen such a thing. <br/> <br/>"Spinning stars," muttered Gordon, "It''s the vidja games the kids play these days, I tell ya."<br/> <br/>Norman nodded in agreement. "Can never understand these newfangled ways muhself."<br/> <br/>The two old trees continued to mutter, but it should be noted that they never stopped watching either.</td>', 'In all their years, the trees had never seen such a thing.  "Spinning stars," muttered Gordon, "It''s the vidja games the kids play these days, I tell ya." Norman nodded in agreement. "Can never understand these newfangled ways muhself." The two old trees continued to mutter, but it should be noted that they never stopped watching either.', '2008-10-01 23:38:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(4986030, 717225, 97166, '<td valign="top">Greg never understood why he took his family on these outings.  He was scared to death of bridges, could never cross one without a bit of vertigo. It mattered not that the ground was only a few feet below.  This was a good thing, of course, as moments later Greg had to be fished out of the swamp.</td>', 'Greg never understood why he took his family on these outings.  He was scared to death of bridges, could never cross one without a bit of vertigo. It mattered not that the ground was only a few feet below.  This was a good thing, of course, as moments later Greg had to be fished out of the swamp.', '2008-10-01 23:39:35.000000', NULL, 1),
