(4988039, 726401, 62187, '<td valign="top">''AB IRATO - Civil Law. Lat. phrase which signifies by a man in anger. It is applied to bequests or gifts, which a man makes adverse to the interest of his heir, in consequence of anger or hatred against him. Thus a devise made under these circumstances is called a testament ab irato. And the suit which the heirs institute to annul this will is called an action ab irato.<br/> <br/>Are you mad about the fence? Anyway, the photo is pretty cool: 8</td>', '''AB IRATO - Civil Law. Lat. phrase which signifies by a man in anger. It is applied to bequests or gifts, which a man makes adverse to the interest of his heir, in consequence of anger or hatred against him. Thus a devise made under these circumstances is called a testament ab irato. And the suit which the heirs institute to annul this will is called an action ab irato. Are you mad about the fence? Anyway, the photo is pretty cool: 8', '2008-10-02 20:04:14.000000', NULL, 1),
