(4988698, 723062, 84907, '<td valign="top">I really like the use of negative space in the shot.  I am sure you will get both good and bad comments on that, but I personally like it and think it adds quite a bit to the interest of the shot.  I also like the way you have used the lighting to give it a more moody feel.  Based upon how clear the triangle is I am assuming a Rembrandt set up.  The triangle is just a bit wide for my taste (probably should only be as wide as the eye at its widest) but there will be lots of folks who probably won''t even recognize the effort, time, and intentionality of the setup.  Technically very very good.  I would love to see your eyes give some feeling, but is for me is all about the tech work that went in.</td>', 'I really like the use of negative space in the shot.  I am sure you will get both good and bad comments on that, but I personally like it and think it adds quite a bit to the interest of the shot.  I also like the way you have used the lighting to give it a more moody feel.  Based upon how clear the triangle is I am assuming a Rembrandt set up.  The triangle is just a bit wide for my taste (probably should only be as wide as the eye at its widest) but there will be lots of folks who probably won''t even recognize the effort, time, and intentionality of the setup.  Technically very very good.  I would love to see your eyes give some feeling, but is for me is all about the tech work that went in.', '2008-10-03 00:49:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(4988704, 727105, 84907, '<td valign="top">:)  been there seen this nice capture.  Thanks for bringing back good Seattle memories!</td>', ':)  been there seen this nice capture.  Thanks for bringing back good Seattle memories!', '2008-10-03 00:50:34.000000', NULL, 1),
