(4997691, 723892, 97166, '<td valign="top">He put his head in his hands in despair. Something that used to be so simple, was now so out of reach.  Smacking the table in anger, followed by a tear of pure frustration, he struggled so hard to remember.  So hard to recollect.<br/> <br/>As his nurse came to place a blanket around his shoulders and lead him into bed, the tears fell a little more freely.  Perhaps tomorrow it would return to him. Sometimes it did, you know. Sometimes it was like he was 20 again.  Today, however, was not that day, and as he drifted off to sleep, sorrow in his heart and frustration in his brain, he prayed to whatever would hear him that tomorrow would be that day.<br/> <br/>That tomorrow he''d be able to remember his daughter''s name once again.</td>', 'He put his head in his hands in despair. Something that used to be so simple, was now so out of reach.  Smacking the table in anger, followed by a tear of pure frustration, he struggled so hard to remember.  So hard to recollect. As his nurse came to place a blanket around his shoulders and lead him into bed, the tears fell a little more freely.  Perhaps tomorrow it would return to him. Sometimes it did, you know. Sometimes it was like he was 20 again.  Today, however, was not that day, and as he drifted off to sleep, sorrow in his heart and frustration in his brain, he prayed to whatever would hear him that tomorrow would be that day. That tomorrow he''d be able to remember his daughter''s name once again.', '2008-10-07 22:24:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(4997692, 725990, 91131, '<td valign="top">spectaculor</td>', 'spectaculor', '2008-10-07 22:25:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(4997695, 725368, 97166, '<td valign="top">The road led ever onward.  No matter how many goals that one reached, the road began again.  Today''s goal was a peak, in the distance.  It looked like the ending, but it was a mirage.  For at that peak would be a path that led away, and such as it was with life.  No matter where you decided your end would be, another path would beckon.<br/> <br/>Charles smiled and started the truck. To this ending then, where he''d find a new beginning.</td>', 'The road led ever onward.  No matter how many goals that one reached, the road began again.  Today''s goal was a peak, in the distance.  It looked like the ending, but it was a mirage.  For at that peak would be a path that led away, and such as it was with life.  No matter where you decided your end would be, another path would beckon. Charles smiled and started the truck. To this ending then, where he''d find a new beginning.', '2008-10-07 22:27:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(4997698, 723441, 97166, '<td valign="top">She clutched the blanket to her and struggled to breathe.  For a moment she was unsure, it had seemed so real.  For a moment it seemed as if it was still after her, but the glow of the lamp assured her it was not.  <br/> <br/>With a deep breath, and the return of all her senses, she realized it had all been just a dream.  A horrible, frightening dream, but a dream.  As her heart slowed, and her breathing settled down, she allowed herself to sink back onto the pillow and close her eyes.  <br/> <br/>This time, it didn''t return.</td>', 'She clutched the blanket to her and struggled to breathe.  For a moment she was unsure, it had seemed so real.  For a moment it seemed as if it was still after her, but the glow of the lamp assured her it was not.   With a deep breath, and the return of all her senses, she realized it had all been just a dream.  A horrible, frightening dream, but a dream.  As her heart slowed, and her breathing settled down, she allowed herself to sink back onto the pillow and close her eyes.   This time, it didn''t return.', '2008-10-07 22:29:49.000000', NULL, 1),
