(5000142, 721302, 41554, '<td valign="top">Parabéns!!! Fantástica imagem. Grande viagem até Wales, mas valeu a pena. Acho que pelo menos aqui no DPC não vi ainda uma imagem HDR que parecesse tão natural e "limpa".<br/>Já agora, gosto muito do teu novo nome!<br/> <br/>E agora, para os nossos amigos que só falam /lêem Inglês...<br/> <br/>Congratulations!! Fantastic image. A long trip to Wales, but boy was it worth it. I think that at least here on DPC I haven''t seen an HDR image that looks so natural and "clean".<br/>By the way, love your "new" name!<br/></td>', 'Parabéns!!! Fantástica imagem. Grande viagem até Wales, mas valeu a pena. Acho que pelo menos aqui no DPC não vi ainda uma imagem HDR que parecesse tão natural e "limpa".Já agora, gosto muito do teu novo nome! E agora, para os nossos amigos que só falam /lêem Inglês... Congratulations!! Fantastic image. A long trip to Wales, but boy was it worth it. I think that at least here on DPC I haven''t seen an HDR image that looks so natural and "clean".By the way, love your "new" name!', '2008-10-08 17:07:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(5000144, 720814, 60173, '<td valign="top">I looked at a few pages of photos that placed higher than this image, and I probably would have placed it higher. As for what went wrong, I''m not really sure. <br/> <br/>I do get the feeling that I want to pull out and turn the image to an angle, but I also realize that wouldn''t be what you were going for. The colors also seem a little cold for what DPC voters usually go for. I played with just contrast, and bumping it +20 makes the eyes really stand out.<br/> <br/>I wonder if it''s a psychological reaction. Maybe the voters just aren''t used to looking at frog eyes. Maybe they were unconsciously wanting the eyes to be facing forward like Kermit. <br/> <br/>The more I look at the image while trying to focus on the eyes, the more the image splits in half, and I don''t see the eyes at all. I look straight up the middle and see nothing; not even the cute little froggy nostrils. That might explain my initial reaction in the first paragraph of wanting to pull out and turn to the side.</td>', 'I looked at a few pages of photos that placed higher than this image, and I probably would have placed it higher. As for what went wrong, I''m not really sure.  I do get the feeling that I want to pull out and turn the image to an angle, but I also realize that wouldn''t be what you were going for. The colors also seem a little cold for what DPC voters usually go for. I played with just contrast, and bumping it +20 makes the eyes really stand out. I wonder if it''s a psychological reaction. Maybe the voters just aren''t used to looking at frog eyes. Maybe they were unconsciously wanting the eyes to be facing forward like Kermit.  The more I look at the image while trying to focus on the eyes, the more the image splits in half, and I don''t see the eyes at all. I look straight up the middle and see nothing; not even the cute little froggy nostrils. That might explain my initial reaction in the first paragraph of wanting to pull out and turn to the side.', '2008-10-08 17:09:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(5000146, 720814, 27133, '<td valign="top">Arrrrrrrrrrrrgggggggggggghhhhhhhhhhhhhhh frogggggggs!</td>', 'Arrrrrrrrrrrrgggggggggggghhhhhhhhhhhhhhh frogggggggs!', '2008-10-08 17:11:11.000000', NULL, 0),
