(5006908, 726427, 49773, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by citymars:</b></div><hr/><i>is it a self-portrait? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Nope. I was the train driver.<br/> <br/>:-)</td>', 'Originally posted by citymars:is it a self-portrait?   Nope. I was the train driver. :-)', '2008-10-13 16:13:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(5006949, 722048, 68947, '<td valign="top">Lady Ettie...Earl''s wife, was out shopping when she caught sight of a woman bearing a camera.  <br/> <br/>"Oooooo, you get that camera away from me, Woman!" she exclaimed with a look of total shock and disdain.  "Don''t you take that picture of me right now.  I forgot to put on my mascara today!"<br/> <br/>The lady photographer smiled and put the camera up to take the shot anyways.  <br/> <br/>"I''m serious now, Girl...don''t you go takin'' no picture of me without my mascara!"<br/> <br/>Feeling a little odd now, the photographer lowered her camera for a moment.  "Lady Ettie, you have so many colorful things on now, no one will notice that you''re not wearing your mascara today."<br/> <br/>Lady Ettie stood back for a moment and looked at the photographer as though she had no brains in her head.  <br/> <br/>"Why," Lady Ettie exclaimed with a puzzled look upon her face, "do you think that I am wearing all of this stuff?"  <br/> <br/>Confused, the photographer shrugged her shoulders, not knowing the answer.<br/> <br/>"BECAUSE," Lady Ettie responded with a type of bewilderment at the photographer''s stupidity...."people are so amazed by my clothing that they don''t notice that I didn''t put on my mascara, of course!"  <br/> <br/></td>', 'Lady Ettie...Earl''s wife, was out shopping when she caught sight of a woman bearing a camera.   "Oooooo, you get that camera away from me, Woman!" she exclaimed with a look of total shock and disdain.  "Don''t you take that picture of me right now.  I forgot to put on my mascara today!" The lady photographer smiled and put the camera up to take the shot anyways.   "I''m serious now, Girl...don''t you go takin'' no picture of me without my mascara!" Feeling a little odd now, the photographer lowered her camera for a moment.  "Lady Ettie, you have so many colorful things on now, no one will notice that you''re not wearing your mascara today." Lady Ettie stood back for a moment and looked at the photographer as though she had no brains in her head.   "Why," Lady Ettie exclaimed with a puzzled look upon her face, "do you think that I am wearing all of this stuff?"   Confused, the photographer shrugged her shoulders, not knowing the answer. "BECAUSE," Lady Ettie responded with a type of bewilderment at the photographer''s stupidity...."people are so amazed by my clothing that they don''t notice that I didn''t put on my mascara, of course!"   ', '2008-10-13 17:03:08.000000', NULL, 0);
